      "claim": "Under common law, force used to retain possession or facilitate escape immediately after the taking elevates larceny to robbery.",
      "evidence": "Robbery is defined as larceny committed by force or threat of force. The 'continuing offense' doctrine treats the taking and the immediate flight as a single transaction; force used during this continuous act satisfies the robbery element.",
